{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":true,"decision":"pass","reasons":[],"slug":"jx76-gog","displayName":"Google Workspace CLI (gog)","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/jx-76/skills/jx76-gog","publisherHandle":"jx-76","publisherDisplayName":"jjx","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/jx-76","version":"1.0.1","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1773767861727,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/jx76-gog/card?ownerHandle=jx-76&version=1.0.1","sha256":"3f3c3acb9d1cda1387f4f6f701465549601dff999686e8ad5b777a649b332d4e","size":1724,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"a23b436e8b614fbb532cf2ade2d64973dd7738f92b677f31e284d15c2c69cc66","bundleFingerprints":["a84e62d601bbb04bdbe1f7923e159f307aada6fcb4f500de2ed987ddabf54fbb","a6b6e7aefb2ebbef44b4a46f92fef8566cbb1fc92ec3097bd3da2e53e7ab70cb"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1842,"sha256":"64a9e317ea4aae8e062f06c34913239ced80cfe0dfb4e54ba31375c7c7dbebfc","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":122,"sha256":"cc6641f746e2ad6348328f8f8f4bae6abdafb2245bc9e9a9e7d7bfd0e91752e5","contentType":"application/json"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"clean","passed":true,"rawStatus":"clean","verdict":"benign","confidence":"medium","summary":"This skill is a straightforward guide for using a Google Workspace CLI, with sensitive OAuth access that is disclosed and user-directed.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789188269200,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unpinned Third-Party Homebrew Dependency"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"SKILL.md"},"region":{"startLine":7,"endLine":7}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"90d8009643d0998c"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `SKILL.md`, line 7  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Supply-chain risk from a mutable third-party package source  \n  **Risk Level**: Medium\n\n  **Complete Code Snippet**:\n\n  ```yaml\n  metadata: {\"clawdbot\":{\"emoji\":\"🎮\",\"requires\":{\"bins\":[\"gog\"],\"install\":[{\"id\":\"brew\",\"kind\":\"brew\",\"formula\":\"steipete/tap/gogcli\",\"bins\":[\"gog\"],\"label\":\"Install gog (brew)\"}]}}}\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The skill directs the environment to install `gogcli` from the third-party Homebrew tap `steipete/tap`. The dependency declaration does not pin an immutable release, formula revision, source commit, or artifact checksum. Consequently, the code installed in the future can differ from what existed when this skill was reviewed.\n\n  Because the project contains no local implementation of the CLI, its effective behavior cannot be verified from the audited package. If the external tap, formula, upstream release process, or referenced artifact is compromised, a modified dependency could execute attacker-controlled code during installation or later CLI invocation.\n\n  This risk is amplified by the documented workflow, which asks users to authorize the installed CLI for Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Contacts, Sheets, and Docs.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. An attacker compromises the third-party Homebrew tap, its maintainer account, the upstream release channel, or an artifact referenced by the formula.\n  2. The attacker modifies the formula or distributed artifact to install a malicious `gog` executable or run malicious installation logic.\n  3. The skill installation process resolves the mutable `steipete/tap/gogcli` dependency without validating a project-declared immutable version or checksum.\n  4. The user follows the documented setup and supplies OAuth client credentials or authorizes one or more Google Workspace services.\n  5. The compromised executable runs with the invoking user's local privileges and may misuse the OAuth authorization available to it.\n  6. Depending on granted scopes, the attacker may access or alter Workspace data, including email, calendar events, Drive files, contacts, spreadsheets, and documents.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  A successfully compromised dependency could execute code with the privileges of the user running Homebrew or invoking `gog`. It could potentially read locally accessible files and authentication material, alter user-owned data, or establish outbound communication subject to host controls.\n\n  After OAuth authorization, the potential cloud impact is bounded by the scopes and Google accounts granted to the CLI. With all services shown in the documentation enabled, affected data could include Gmail messages, calendars, Drive content, contacts, Sheets, and Docs. The audited files do not demonstrate that such a compromise currently exists; this finding concerns the absence of controls against a mutable supply-chain dependency.","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Pin the dependency to an immutable, reviewed release rather than relying only on the mutable formula name.\n  2. Verify downloaded artifacts with a cryptographic checksum or signature tied to the pinned release.\n  3. Record the authoritative upstream repository and expected release provenance in the skill metadata or documentation.\n  4. Prefer a vendor-controlled, reproducible distribution channel where available, and review the Homebrew formula before enabling automated installation.\n  5. Add dependency monitoring so formula ownership, source URLs, checksums, and release signatures are revalidated when versions change.\n  6. Apply least privilege to OAuth authorization: request only the specific Google Workspace services and scopes required for the intended task.\n  7. Store OAuth credentials in an operating-system credential store with restrictive permissions, and document procedures for reviewing and revoking granted access.\n  8. In managed environments, install an independently verified binary through an approved internal package repository."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":75,"primaryLanguage":"JSON","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789188205.478601,"endTime":1789188239.1661775}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"gog","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57dj1cypmf05287gs0dgxw4yn8e9jqx-ogOj0b/clawscan-skillspector-619380306/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-12T04:43:24.609749+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":17,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":37,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1842,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"_meta.json","type":"json","lines":6,"executable":false,"size_bytes":122,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-edb90d2d2c9a42c580cf4d5a9239f6d3","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_line":null},"finding":"secret.json","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"Use `gog` for Gmail/Calendar/Drive/Contacts/Sheets/Docs. Requires OAuth setup.\n\nSetup (once)\n- `gog auth credentials /path/to/client_secret.json`\n- `gog auth add you@gmail.com --services gmail,calendar,drive,contacts,sheets,docs`\n- `gog auth list`\n","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"63042cd4992adaaec8b31491f464e5489ca94eee3632bd7658e9d44e00ab4cb8","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":14,"end_lin